<title>JAPAN: Motorola, Mitsubishi to sell PCs in Japan.</title>
<headline>Motorola, Mitsubishi to sell PCs in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc and Mitsubishi Corp. have agreed to join forces to enter the Japanese computer market, a business newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The companies will start sales of Motorola-brand personal computers (PCs), which are compatible with Macintosh series Apple Computer Inc., by the end of the year, the daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said.</p>
<p>Motorola will start production by the year's end of PCs equipped with Power PC microprocessor units under licence with the Apple Macintosh.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi will distribute the PCs made by Motorola, targeting sales of 210,000 PCs, or 42 billion yen, in the first year, the newspaper said.</p>
